About Volvo Autonomous Solutions (V.A.S.)
The autonomous transport solution offered by Volvo Autonomous Solutions includes
a vehicle purpose-built for autonomous driving, a virtual driver, required
infrastructure, operations, and uptime support as well as a cloud solution that
controls the transport system and manages logistics flows. The solutions
developed by V.A.S. are tailor-made for customers' needs and intended to make
their operations safer, more productive, and more sustainable.

About Waabi
Waabi, founded by AI visionary Raquel Urtasun, is building the defining Physical
AI Platform, starting with autonomous transportation. Waabi's autonomous
trucking technology already moves freight across Texas, adding safe, reliable
capacity and supporting on-time deliveries for Fortune 50 customers. The company
is expanding into robotaxis and will deploy at least 25,000 on the Uber platform
in the coming years. Waabi has raised over $1.3 billion to date and is backed by
and partnered with world leaders in AI, automotive, logistics, and deep tech,
including Khosla Ventures, NVIDIA, Volvo Group Venture Capital, and Uber.

About Warp
Warp is building the technology platform for a more connected freight industry.
Serving customers including Walmart, DoorDash, and Gopuff, Warp brings
less-than-truckload (LTL) and full-truckload (FTL) transportation into a single
network. Its model combines the scale of a distributed carrier network with
centralized intelligence and execution, creating a platform that can expand with
customer demand and incorporate new capacity, including autonomous trucks.

